                    "The sequence of statements is the whole story.  Dior's creative director Jonathan Anderson told WWD the film was \"all hand-drawn using techniques that go back to the 1940s.\"  Chomet, the director, then told Variety on 7 November that they \"used an automated interpolation system for a very small part of the process,\" interpolation being software that generates the in-between frames that join two drawings.  On the anatomy, Chomet's explanation was that \"you might see six or seven fingers because you're trying to convey movement.\"  Dior has neither confirmed nor denied; Adweek reports three outlets asked and got no response.  The end credits list no software involvement.",
