                    "TikTok Shop Plus began rolling out over the weekend to <mark>more than one million</mark> of TikTok's most loyal United States shoppers.  It costs <mark>9.99 dollars a month after a 30-day free trial</mark>, against 14.99 for Amazon Prime and 12.95 for Walmart Plus.  Members get three coupons a month, <mark>5 dollars off with no minimum, 10 dollars off orders of 59 dollars or more, and 30 dollars off orders of 119 dollars or more</mark>, plus 10 percent off selected products, free shipping on items carrying a Plus badge, and instant store-credit refunds on qualifying products up to twice a month.  TikTok's president of strategic initiatives Patrick Nommensen says it is \"currently being piloted with an expanding group of eligible U.S. users.\"",
                    "Two mechanisms sit inside that.  The free shipping attaches to badged items, not to the member, so TikTok has created a tier where badged products get preferential conversion among its highest-intent shoppers.  And those coupon thresholds are basket engineering: 59 and 119 dollars reward whoever happens to have a product priced just above them.",
